        chords: [],
        description: "If you're pretty new to blues, the progression goes like so: INTRO x 1 A PHRASE x 1 B PHRASE x 1 A PHRASE x 1 TURNAROUND x 1 Then every other time through will go like so: A PHRASE x 2 B PHRASE x 1 A PHRASE x 1 TURNAROUND x 1 NOTE: The F#7(#9) and the E9 in the turn around are STRUMMED. I chose not to include the strumming pattern, because I feel like it wouldn't translate very well on tablature anyway. Just make something up that goes along with the rhythm. Trust me, you can do it! Enjoy!"
